# Kumbi routing — default k3s (Traefik + flannel + servicelb).
#
# Default k3s stack:
#   CNI          → flannel (VXLAN, kube-system, DaemonSet)
#   LoadBalancer → servicelb / klipper-lb (kube-system, svclb-traefik)
#   Ingress      → Traefik (kube-system/traefik, Service type LoadBalancer)
#                  IngressClass `traefik` routes to ClusterIP Services.
#
#   Ingress `kumbi` (ingressClassName: traefik) — host ${DOMAIN}
#     /api            → service backend:8080
#     /app/storage    → service backend:8080
#     /               → service frontend:80
#   Plus:
#     api.${DOMAIN} / → service backend:8080
#     www.${DOMAIN} / → service frontend:80
#
# TLS is terminated in Traefik using the kumbi-tls secret (mkcert for dev/test,
# cert-manager for staging, supplied for prod) via Ingress.spec.tls.
#
# REACHABILITY (k3s node host IP, Traefik via servicelb):
#   https://kumbi.test/       → node :443  → Traefik (LoadBalancer) → frontend
#   https://kumbi.test/api    → node :443  → Traefik → backend:8080
#   https://api.kumbi.test/   → node :443  → Traefik → backend:8080
#   (ports 80/443 are Traefik's LoadBalancer ports fulfilled by servicelb;
#    custom ports can be set via INGRESS_HTTP_PORT/INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT in
#    kumbi-app-config, but default is 80/443.)
#
# Optional host nginx passthrough (infra/host/nginx-stream.conf) is generally
# NOT needed — Traefik already binds 80/443 via servicelb.
#
# Verify: `make ports ENV=dev` shows Traefik + Ingress → Services;
#         `make k3s-check ENV=dev` confirms flannel + servicelb + traefik.
